+### gateway prune
+
+```text
+ai-ctl gateway prune --keep <N>
+```
+
+Removes every llama-swap release but the `N` newest and the current one, which is always kept,
+and prints what it removed and the megabytes freed. Nothing is removed when the running gateway
+runs one of the releases to remove: the error names `ai-ctl down` then `ai-ctl up`, which restart
+it on the current release. A removal that fails stops the prune, and its error names the releases
+removed before it.
+
+| Option | Value | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `--keep` | `N`, zero or more | required | How many of the newest releases to keep, besides the current one |
+
+```bash
+ai-ctl gateway prune --keep 1
+```
